//! run
//! since: 1.0.0
//! stdout:
//! | |    42|42    |  42   |-42|+42|0xff|FF|101|0o10|
//! | |000042|-00042|00,001,234|0_001_234|1,234,567|***7|
//! | |3.14|3|0.13|2.67|1.234500e+03|25.000000%|     1.5|
// §12 rule 11 (Lyric 5 12 §2 rules 1–3): an integer takes fill, alignment, sign, `#`, `0`,
// width, grouping and a radix; a float all but `#` and a radix, with a precision and its forms —
// rounded half away from zero on the value's exact binary digits, so `2.675` is `2.67`.
println(f"|{42:>6}|{42:<6}|{42:^7}|{-42:+}|{42:+}|{255:#x}|{255:X}|{5:b}|{8:#o}|")
println(f"|{42:06}|{-42:06}|{1234:010,}|{1234:08_}|{1234567:,}|{7:*>4}|")
println(f"|{3.14159:.2}|{2.5:.0f}|{0.125:.2f}|{2.675:.2f}|{1234.5:e}|{0.25:%}|{1.5:>8.1}|")
